WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.620
You began as a single cell,
holding 46 chromosomes.

2
00:00:04.670 --> 00:00:08.250
Each of your parents has 46
in their body cells, too.

3
00:00:08.300 --> 00:00:11.420
Simply add them together,
and you'd have 92.

4
00:00:11.470 --> 00:00:13.900
The next generation would double again.

5
00:00:13.950 --> 00:00:18.660
Yet the number stays at 46,
generation after generation.

6
00:00:18.710 --> 00:00:21.430
So how is it halved so exactly?

7
00:00:21.480 --> 00:00:25.460
In this mission, you'll follow one
cell through two divisions in a row,

8
00:00:25.510 --> 00:00:28.120
and count what each new cell holds.

9
00:00:28.170 --> 00:00:32.540
Then you'll set it beside mitosis, and
compare the cells that each kind of division

10
00:00:32.590 --> 00:00:33.600
makes.

11
00:00:33.650 --> 00:00:38.270
Your mission: find out how the
chromosome number is halved so exactly.
